<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūrāmentum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				hardening</i> in concreto. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a hardened</i>, i. e.
				<i>ligneous vine-branch</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 21,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 17, 23, 35, § 208</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 12,
			1</span></i>.—Called also duramen, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 22,
				1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a means of
				hardening</i>, <i>stimulus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humanae imbecillitatis efficacissimum
					duramentum est necessitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 2, 7, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>firmness</i> (with
			robur), <i><span class="en">Sen. Tranq. An. 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
